# Mission plan

## Objectives

1. Register a new top-level documentation folder in
   **`.sedea/documentation-management.yaml`** with **`localPath`** and rclone
   **`remote`** / **`remotePath`** per
   [`.sedea/centers/documentation-management/rules/00_documentation-management.mdc`](../../rules/00_documentation-management.mdc).
2. Create the local folder under the hosting workspace and add it to the
   hosting-repo **`.gitignore`** so documentation payloads stay out of git.
3. Guide the user to choose a **Google Drive** folder and capture the remote
   link/path they provide (GDrive is the only provider in v1).
4. Emit an OS-appropriate rclone setup **command** (or short script text) that
   requires the user’s **own Google Drive OAuth `client_id` / `client_secret`**
   (rclone’s shared Drive `client_id` is retiring during 2026), and instruct
   them to run it in the **VS Code / Cursor integrated terminal** (copy/paste) —
   auth and browser consent cannot run inside the agent session.
5. After the user confirms the setup command succeeded, run an agent **dry-run**
   as the **exit of installation** and report that result; then a **full pull**
   sync only after explicit confirm.
6. Close the dispatch with an explicit Squad Leader resolution proposal when
   configuration and sync gates are complete or abandoned.

